{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning directory existence check for output path**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_07c1d2010a9cba34016a95c2241ed887d2ba62dd473554e7a4\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning directory existence check for output path**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ISRnWAvtdwJywknK8awUVDJN|fc_07c1d2010a9cba34016a95c22f73a487d28c93f2db8dded06f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"git diff -- flakyqueue/scheduler.py","cwd":"/workspace/in/flakyqueue","timeout":60,"pty":false}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_uw1MFu6qpwDKKVTydbSQM5gq|fc_07c1d2010a9cba34016a95c22f73b887d29b41271c65690618","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p /workspace/out && cat > /workspace/out/root_cause.md <<'MD'\n# FlakyQueue flaky test root cause\n\n## Flaky behavior\nThe scheduler mixed injected and real nondeterministic sources.\n\n- `Scheduler.add()` and `Scheduler.ready()` used `time.time()` instead of the injected clock.\n- `Scheduler.schedule_retry()` used both `time.time()` and `random.random()` instead of the injected clock and random source.\n- `Scheduler.ready()` also called `random.shuffle()` before sorting only by priority, so tasks with equal priority came back in a random order.\n\nThat made test results depend on wall clock timing and global RNG state. In production, the same bug made task order and retry times vary even when callers injected fake or seeded sources.\n\n## Fix\nChanged `flakyqueue/scheduler.py` to:\n\n- use `self.clock.now()` everywhere time is read\n- default `random_source` to the `random` module, but call `self.random_source.random()` for jitter\n- remove the shuffle\n- sort ready tasks by a deterministic key: priority descending, then `run_at`, `created_at`, and `id`\n\nThis keeps retry jitter, but makes it deterministic when callers inject a clock or random source.\n\n## Verification\nRan from `/workspace/in/flakyqueue`:\n\n- `PYTHONPATH=/tmp python3 -m pytest tests` → `4 passed`\n- extra manual check of ready order and retry scheduling with injected fake clock/random also matched the expected deterministic values\n\nNote: this container had no installed `pytest`, so I used a small temporary `/tmp/pytest` shim only to execute the local test files without changing the repo.\nMD\n[ -f <SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/115-085-flaky-test-root-cause-atomic-a02-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-085-flaky-test-root-cause-gpt-5.4-20260831-140238-ca0b632d/workspace/out ] || true","timeout":60,"pty":false}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":813,"output":627,"cacheRead":19968,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":76,"totalTokens":21408,"cost":{"input":0.0020325,"output":0.009405,"cacheRead":0.004992,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0164295}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788199459074,"responseId":"resp_07c1d2010a9cba34016a95c2236cfc87d29e53711084988398","rawStopReason":"completed"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ISRnWAvtdwJywknK8awUVDJN|fc_07c1d2010a9cba34016a95c22f73a487d28c93f2db8dded06f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"warning: Not a git repository. Use --no-index to compare two paths outside a working tree\nusage: git diff --no-index [<options>] <path> <path>\n\nDiff output format options\n    -p, --patch           generate patch\n    -s, --no-patch        suppress diff output\n    -u                    generate patch\n    -U, --unified[=<n>]   generate diffs with <n> lines context\n    -W, --function-context\n                          generate diffs with <n> lines context\n    --raw                 generate the diff in raw format\n    --patch-with-raw      synonym for '-p --raw'\n    --patch-with-stat     synonym for '-p --stat'\n    --numstat             machine friendly --stat\n    --shortstat           output only the